# SABOTAGE: PP-5 (Batch 2 TENANT-ROLE) / the :identity_namespace enumerating guard — MIS-WIRE
# pawchart's `@current_org_labels` `:identity_namespace` seam to the Billing scope itself, which
# materializes no Membership. The tenant-plane Billing surface can then no longer resolve the
# caller's REAL per-org Membership role (the `PawChart.Operator` spine is no longer named), so the
# role-gated billing writes fail CLOSED for EVERYONE — a clinic ADMIN can no longer
# subscribe/manage-payment — reintroducing the Batch-2 silent-breakage class. Both the enumerating
# guard (the wired namespace no longer MATERIALIZES identity) and the admin positive control FLIP.
#
# RE-ANCHORED (2026-10-23): this patch used to DELETE the label. Since 53eae0cc the framework's
# `Samen.Web.Router.__assert_tenant_identity_seam__/4` refuses to COMPILE an armable tenant mount of
# a guarded surface that names no `:identity_namespace`, so the deletion produced a compile error
# ("suite failed but no test-failure headers found") instead of a named-test flip. The compile guard
# asserts the label's PRESENCE; the enumerating guard below asserts its SUBSTANCE — that the named
# namespace materializes `User`/`Membership`. Mis-wiring keeps the host compiling and refutes the
# load-bearing half: the beacon still looks wired, and the role still collapses to `:member` for a
# real admin. Reverts byte-exact.
# APP: pawchart
# TEST_FILES: test/billing_role_gate_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: wires :identity_namespace to an identity-materializing namespace
# MUST_FAIL: an ADMIN resolves the admin billing actor
diff --git a/pawchart/lib/pawchart_web/router.ex b/pawchart/lib/pawchart_web/router.ex
--- a/pawchart/lib/pawchart_web/router.ex
+++ b/pawchart/lib/pawchart_web/router.ex
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@
     org_directory: {PawChart.Directory, :orgs, []},
     authn: {:app_env, :pawchart, :auth_required?},
